{"title":"2023 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 14","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(Rectangular_Form,_similar_to_Solution_1)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (Rectangular Form, similar to Solution 1)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_5_(with_motivation)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 5 (with motivation)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Power_Solve\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Power Solve</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_OmegaLearn\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by OmegaLearn</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">10</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>How many complex numbers satisfy the equation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/8/f/68f57ab9d312f4ef1c0af670fd263a32facbae18.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z^5=\\overline{z}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"52\" height=\"17\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/b/f3b8023032c1d94aa923383802ca03df3b4315df.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{z}$\" width=\"9\" height=\"11\" /> is the conjugate of the complex number <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/3/b13f21416d84e13708696f34dea81026cda583c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/c/2ac2973816ccb454c5ae2b19b01ec42730fee44e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)} ~2\\qquad\\textbf{(B)} ~3\\qquad\\textbf{(C)} ~5\\qquad\\textbf{(D)} ~6\\qquad\\textbf{(E)} ~7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"351\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>When <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/8/f/68f57ab9d312f4ef1c0af670fd263a32facbae18.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z^5=\\overline{z}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"52\" height=\"17\" />, there are two conditions: either <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/2/0/72079803c6fcdcfa95b6d7f383f6ad71f1eb631b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z=0$\" width=\"42\" height=\"12\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/8/2/682d15d010bda1c163816c22f92c6024c41b8ce1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z\\neq 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"42\" height=\"17\" />. When <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/8/2/682d15d010bda1c163816c22f92c6024c41b8ce1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z\\neq 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"42\" height=\"17\" />, since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/8/cd8d3cd9929228103a259650d42f7100b4953ad7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|z^5|=|\\overline{z}|$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"72\" height=\"21\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/f/01f7aac3e57f997317789dcd4368f8a7b07ebc24.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|z|=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"51\" height=\"18\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/4/1644ddf092d6135a403a3d24065e6f05942a8738.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z^5\\cdot z=z^6=\\overline{z}\\cdot z=|z|^2=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"222\" height=\"21\" />. Consider the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/4/5/44538a0e632a0774ca61139d6d1f69288d870cf7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r(\\cos \\theta +i\\sin \\theta)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"127\" height=\"20\" /> form, when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/d/dfdf1229b1b033d1fd3ace6595f2e9799bcf6aca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z^6=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"52\" height=\"17\" />, there are 6 different solutions for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/3/b13f21416d84e13708696f34dea81026cda583c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />. Therefore, the number of complex numbers satisfying <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/e/32eb27d8280646c66f283c0d94b7bab7b4cc8cf5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z^5=\\bar{z}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"52\" height=\"17\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/4/be46fea85dd041f3a076ad81ab2f43e62bfb4442.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(E)} 7}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"48\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p><p>~plasta\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/2/c723eb90729414ceb3eb6d6631413c4b43f1d2cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z = re^{i\\theta}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"70\" height=\"17\" /> We now have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/4/8c4979f7fb60c660dd895a776b9b9df394fde8ef.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{z} = re^{-i\\theta},$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"80\" height=\"21\" /> and want to solve \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/4/5/14529c73e17ca03d43b583f99392aca91cd073a7.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[r^5e^{5i\\theta} = re^{-i\\theta}.\\]\" width=\"110\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p>From this, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/5/545933c25a1802d9dbcfc24ab4c013d07ef4ccbc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r = 0$\" width=\"41\" height=\"12\" /> as a solution, which gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/9/aa9f0d97d2f39f78f05e05da40bf04f5a7c0726c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" />. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/4/e1445a4a08526d540eb1c02a5a00115f69bdc426.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r\\neq 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"41\" height=\"17\" />, then we divide by it, yielding \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/9/4e9161dd2aa856e30c28da6c06711ca4cc72913b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[r^4e^{5i\\theta} = e^{-i\\theta}.\\]\" width=\"102\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p>Dividing both sides by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/c/0ec3093bfe0e9e8011d82ef57b051550a46d3994.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$e^{-i\\theta}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"33\" height=\"17\" /> yields <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/f/79f5e72243f67711a0d4e1b2ffee496f30e318c3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r^4e^{6i\\theta} = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"79\" height=\"17\" />. \nTaking the magnitude of both sides tells us that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/4/d043966599d1bac257859af8a1a5fc55cf65bde8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r^4 = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"51\" height=\"17\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/d/4ed6f9e7893f1db59a13c71b2c1aff61d6fff4f4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r^2 = \\pm 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"65\" height=\"18\" />. However, if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/1/b/61bbee974e1ec5ffbd121bbb4d32db015dcc2066.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r^2 = -1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"65\" height=\"18\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/7/1b76d0950d0bc4288c6325495cfd3fb946f43656.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r = \\pm i$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"52\" height=\"13\" />, but <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> must be real. Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/c/9/1c9d9d65dde4756baa458cbbecb0d22ba5048da9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r^2 = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"51\" height=\"17\" />. \n</p><p>Multiplying both sides by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/2/e2221c84f16a3f75ae07e5023384cc40d9c05357.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r^2$\" width=\"14\" height=\"15\" />, \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/2/482e2efbf2c0971049406a93e949358060ed7586.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[r^6\\cdot e^{6i\\theta} = z^6 = 1.\\]\" width=\"134\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p>Each of the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />th roots of unity is a solution to this, so there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/c/4/5c4eb6b600aac045312975b1e207d023f418b448.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6 + 1 = \\boxed{\\textbf{(E)}\\ 7}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"120\" height=\"30\" /> solutions. \n</p><p>-Benedict T (countmath 1)\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3_.28Rectangular_Form.2C_similar_to_Solution_1.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(Rectangular_Form,_similar_to_Solution_1)\">Solution 3 (Rectangular Form, similar to Solution 1)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (Rectangular Form, similar to Solution 1)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/f/d5fdcd6e4bbde5f0a3289c503472267ec35d37e0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z = a+bi$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"79\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>Then, our equation becomes: \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/d/64d52c12e7e1c0b768217785086a07455523be36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a+bi)^5=a-bi$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"139\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p>Note that since every single term in the expansion contains either an <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" />, simply setting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/c/69cefa6855d2216036df094012f7ad2a7e4e204f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"45\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/4/fc43f0ea59e862d7db01586894e9eea730d427b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"43\" height=\"14\" /> yields a solution.\n</p><p>Now, considering the other case that either <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> does not equal <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />:\n</p><p>Multiplying both sides by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/1/5/615e780fda439b2829922a704a60b31c5ed77191.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+bi$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"45\" height=\"14\" /> (or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/3/b13f21416d84e13708696f34dea81026cda583c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />), we get:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/4/5d431cdbc9cab0f6a6e6efe14857abf085a86517.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a+bi)^6=a^2+b^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"148\" height=\"21\" /> (since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/6/a56bfe567aec24da391224dc2f10e8cc4ef626dc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i^2=-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"63\" height=\"18\" />).\n</p><p>Substituting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/3/b13f21416d84e13708696f34dea81026cda583c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> back into the left hand side, we get:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/5/e050710496beea9c1bac3ca941dc0a98c948a417.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z^6=a^2+b^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"97\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>Note that this will have 6 distinct, non-zero solutions since in this case, we consider that either <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> is not <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, and these are simply the sixth roots of a positive real number.\n</p><p>Adding up the solutions, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/4/b749229d8faa1f380a0383daa07abf2d6e50e400.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1+6=$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"61\" height=\"15\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/4/be46fea85dd041f3a076ad81ab2f43e62bfb4442.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(E)} 7}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"48\" height=\"28\" />\n</p><p>-SwordOfJustice\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4\">Solution 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Using the fact that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/5/bf523c8d600288ee789f84da657762a9854eea0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z\\bar{z}=|z|^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"68\" height=\"19\" />, we rewrite our equation as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/3/6531ece0807b6d7a1dea82801e4b4582eb32eef2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z^6=|z|^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"70\" height=\"21\" />.  Now, let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> represent <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/7/8/77888cf7d3c4635b8bc8c06ee89dc2a2d2f86538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|z|$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"17\" height=\"18\" />. We know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/b/67bed75b9c1ec9db04c4a0877524a7ad8dac4553.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r^6 = r^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"58\" height=\"17\" />; hence, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/9/d19a56bce24f7e9c019d5927fc4ef5e4d1333f45.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r^6-r^2=r^2(r^4-1)=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"192\" height=\"21\" />. \n</p><p>From here, we have two cases: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/0/400365c088499af977542271fc6363b086a63499.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r=0$\" width=\"41\" height=\"12\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/3/1930619a38fceee8e02990ea79026a348193307e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"41\" height=\"12\" />. In the case that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/0/400365c088499af977542271fc6363b086a63499.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r=0$\" width=\"41\" height=\"12\" />, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/c/36c293d1b2e1bc45f56486ecf7e27c4a568e40cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z^6=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"52\" height=\"17\" /> hence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/2/0/72079803c6fcdcfa95b6d7f383f6ad71f1eb631b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z=0$\" width=\"42\" height=\"12\" />. This gives one solution. Alternatively, if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/3/1930619a38fceee8e02990ea79026a348193307e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"41\" height=\"12\" />, then we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/d/dfdf1229b1b033d1fd3ace6595f2e9799bcf6aca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z^6=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"52\" height=\"17\" />, giving <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> solutions for each root of unity.\n</p><p><br />\nTherefore, the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/8/03868e3cd5102b134602779ac0309c242d45bdf3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6+1=$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"61\" height=\"15\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/4/be46fea85dd041f3a076ad81ab2f43e62bfb4442.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(E)} 7}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"48\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p><p><br />\n- xHypotenuse\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_5_.28with_motivation.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_5_(with_motivation)\">Solution 5 (with motivation)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 5 (with motivation)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Immediately, we know that if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/3/b13f21416d84e13708696f34dea81026cda583c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> is a root of unity, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/a/34aad012c852f65e1b61d95bc3de65c5946d349b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\bar{z} = \\frac{1}{z}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"49\" height=\"38\" />. This only holds if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/3/b13f21416d84e13708696f34dea81026cda583c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> is a root of unity of has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/3/1/83147269611ed30c50eb2ddeb1b275003b3ab032.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|z| = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"51\" height=\"18\" />. In addition, if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/3/b13f21416d84e13708696f34dea81026cda583c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> is a root of unity, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/8/9/689a869366b7bce0801a72fdd707a065315ba0ce.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z^n$\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" /> is also a root of unity. So, if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/f/60f94571975d71136975339a9f9deef223cf6d7d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z^5 = \\frac{1}{z}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"56\" height=\"38\" />, we require <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/2/8/728eaf9a93a6a111a69ede7008d2959ecb91ded8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z^6 = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"49\" height=\"15\" />, and that implies all sixth roots of unity. However, 0 is also a solution, hence we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/4/1/94152541528ed008abea53ff30e18a07a3c37f51.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{7}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"20\" height=\"23\" /> values. We can prove no other <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/3/b13f21416d84e13708696f34dea81026cda583c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> can satisfy this requirement as a conjugational rotation on the complex plane is a 180 degree rotation of a point, and no roots of unity besides the sixth roots can map, after a 180 degree rotation, modular 5 to the same point as the conjugate.\n</p><p>~Pinotation\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Power_Solve\">Video Solution by Power Solve</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Power Solve\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/YXIH3UbLqK8?si=l8Ay2f0dMqSkjuQH&amp;t=1975\">https://youtu.be/YXIH3UbLqK8?si=l8Ay2f0dMqSkjuQH&amp;t=1975</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_OmegaLearn\">Video Solution by OmegaLearn</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by OmegaLearn\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/rbdIrmOyczk\">https://youtu.be/rbdIrmOyczk</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/m627Mjp3PkM\">https://youtu.be/m627Mjp3PkM</a>\n</p><p>~Steven Chen (Professor Chen Education Palace, www.professorchenedu.com)\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"2\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_12A\" title=\"2023 AMC 12A\">2023 AMC 12A</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_12A_Problems\" title=\"2023 AMC 12A Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_12A_Answer_Key\" title=\"2023 AMC 12A Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2023 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 13\">Problem 13</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2023 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 15\">Problem 15</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2023 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2023 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2023 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_12A_Proble